  "description": "* (Disclaimer: The content in this video is intended for educational and informational purposes only)\nStockton, California — On Monday, May 4, 2026, at approximately 7:00 a.m., Stockton Police officers responded to the 2000 block of Nevada Street after receiving a report of a suspicious male armed with an axe who was smashing the front door of an occupied residence. Two Stockton Police officers arrived on scene and determined that the suspect, identified as 25-year-old Moises Andrade, attempted to gain entry into the occupied residence and used an axe to cause substantial damage to the front door. Officers also received information indicating that Andrade may have been heading to another residence, where additional acts of violence were believed to be possible. Both officers continued their follow-up investigation and subsequently learned that Andrade was staying nearby at a residence in the 1200 block of Deep Cliff Way. At approximately 7:37 a.m., the officers proceeded to that location and approached on foot. After attempting to contact Andrade at the front door, the garage door partially opened, and they observed Andrade inside. The officers contacted Andrade and began talking to him. While officers were speaking with the Andrade, he retrieved an axe that was tied to his bike, inside the garage, and armed himself in front of the officers. One Officer drew his service weapon, and another officer drew his taser as a less-lethal option. Officers attempted to de-escalate by stepping back and giving direct verbal commands for Andrade to drop the axe. Andrade refused to obey those commands, took a pre-assaultive stance, and raised the axe in a threatening manner, in close proximity to the officers. In response, one officer fired his service weapon, striking Andrade. Officers immediately rendered medical aid to Andrade until CenCal Fire and EMS Authority and Stockton Fire personnel arrived and transported Andrade to an area hospital. Andrade was later pronounced deceased. No officers were injured during this incident.\n\n🚨𝑇ℎ𝑖𝑠 𝑐ℎ𝑎𝑛𝑛𝑒𝑙 𝑝𝑟𝑜𝑣𝑖𝑑𝑒𝑠 𝑐𝑜𝑛𝑡𝑒𝑥𝑡𝑢𝑎𝑙 𝑑𝑜𝑐𝑢𝑚𝑒𝑛𝑡𝑎𝑡𝑖𝑜𝑛 𝑎𝑛𝑑 𝑎𝑛𝑎𝑙𝑦𝑠𝑖𝑠 𝑜𝑓 𝑟𝑒𝑎𝑙 𝑝𝑜𝑙𝑖𝑐𝑒 𝑖𝑛𝑐𝑖𝑑𝑒𝑛𝑡𝑠 𝑢𝑠𝑖𝑛𝑔 𝑝𝑢𝑏𝑙𝑖𝑐𝑙𝑦 𝑎𝑣𝑎𝑖𝑙𝑎𝑏𝑙𝑒 𝑟𝑒𝑐𝑜𝑟𝑑𝑠.\n\n⚠️𝑉𝑖𝑒𝑤𝑒𝑟 𝑑𝑖𝑠𝑐𝑟𝑒𝑡𝑖𝑜𝑛 𝑖𝑠 𝑎𝑑𝑣𝑖𝑠𝑒𝑑 𝑑𝑢𝑒 𝑡𝑜 𝑡ℎ𝑒 𝑠𝑒𝑟𝑖𝑜𝑢𝑠 𝑛𝑎𝑡𝑢𝑟𝑒 𝑜𝑓 𝑡ℎ𝑒 𝑐𝑜𝑛𝑡𝑒𝑛𝑡.⚠️\n\n⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐\nSpecial thanks to Shout-Out Supporters on Patreon:\n- 'DIY Solar Power with Will Prowse'\n- Ahmed Omar Alkahlout\n- KHALID\n- Michael Griffin\n- John Doe\n- 'Twitchypowpow'\n- Lillian Daley\n- Tyrell Robertson\n- christine Grinter\n- 'The Evil Queen'\n- Benjamin Osgood\n- Gary Wilson\n- LJ\n- Edward Aquino\n- Brianna Wilkins\n- William\n- Elisabeth Craig\n- Bobby Roach\n- Sarin Dipity\n- Becky Hopkins\n- thomas\n- Cody Stephens\n- Troy Polansky\n- Tulla Belle\n- 'quadrakyiro'\n- Scott Mackin\n- \"John B. GunsSaveLife\"\n- david wallace\n- Brice Danos\n- 'PhlyDaily'\n- RayJayOB\n- Josef Rex\n- 'Jun'\n- 'Xenik'\n- 'GotsNoGroove Cheryl'\n- Kelly Goodwin\n- 'Dawesenm'\n- Paul Rohrbaugh\n- 'AccuShoot.com'\n- Lisa Overly\n- Gerardo Flores\n- 'coco Coco'\n⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐\n\nSupport us on Patreon: https://www.patreon.com/PoliceActivity\n\n🛍️ Check out our Amazon store: https://www.amazon.com/shop/PoliceActivity 🛍️\n\n- Links to the Best Dash Cams you can buy.\nVIOFO A329S 4K: https://amzn.to/42NUA0I\nVantrue N4 Pro S 4K: https://amzn.to/4cVH5SV\nGarmin X310 4K: https://amzn.to/3QOEz8c\nBlackVue DR970X 4K: https://amzn.to/4tlFj2o\nREDTIGER F17 Elite 4K: https://amzn.to/4tHQymw\nTHINKWARE ARC 700 4K: https://amzn.to/3OBWpuA\n\n- Security Cameras\nArlo Ultra 4K: https://amzn.to/3RgGoe9\neufyCam S3 Pro 4K: https://amzn.to/3QJX25U\nGoogle Nest Cam 2K: https://amzn.to/4up9tCC\nRing Spotlight Cam Pro: https://amzn.to/3P1xD7d\n\nDisclosure: Please note that we will receive a small commission from purchases made through our Amazon store. This is at no cost to you. It helps support our channel and allows us to continue creating content for you. Your support is highly appreciated!\n\nTimestamps:\n0:00 - Bodycam: Officer